json_data = [{"Index":"1","SS / Module":"USB","Test Case Name":"USB_FS_Device_Bulk_Transfer_test","Feature":"FS Device Bulk Transfer","Meta Headers":"<stdio.h>; <stdlib.h>; \"usb.h\"","Meta Macros":"NA","Meta Arrays":"buf_data[16]","Speed":"NA","Mode":"NA","Memory Start Offset":"NA","Memory End Offset":"NA","Meta Test Description":"This testcase validates USB Full-Speed (FS) Device mode Bulk Transfer operation. It begins by calling nic_programming() and enabling all IRQs via GIC_EnableAllIRQ(). Buffer memory regions (Buffer_PointerLO and event_trb_addr) are cleared in a loop of 20 iterations. A soft reset is performed by writing 0x40f00000 to MIZAR_USB_DCTL and polling until MIZAR_USB_DCTL reads 0xf00000. USB2 PHY is configured by writing 0x40002407 to MIZAR_USB_GUSB2PHYCFG. The event ring is set up by writing Default_Event_Ring_Array to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTADRLO, 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTADRHI, 0x30 to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTSIZ, and 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT. MIZAR_USB_GCTL is read and then written with 0x30c12214 for port direction. MIZAR_USB_DCFG is read and written with 0x480801. MIZAR_USB_DEVTEN is written with 0x1f to enable device events. MIZAR_USB_GUCTL is read and written with 0xa400010. Endpoint configuration is performed using set_configuration() for 9 endpoints (START NEW CONFIGURATION followed by 8 endpoint configurations), each writing to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1, MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0, and MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD at various offsets and polling MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD until the command completes. Endpoint TX resource configuration is done in a loop for 8 endpoints, writing 0x1 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0+(i0x10) and 0x402 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+(i0x10), polling until command completes. MIZAR_USB_DALEPENA is written with 0x3 to enable physical endpoints 0 and 1. MIZAR_USB_DCTL is written with 0x80f00000 to run the device. MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN0 is written with 0x80000000 to enable sysreg interrupt. The test then waits for link state connect/reset events via interrupt pending flags. MIZAR_USB_DCFG is rewritten. Enumeration marker 0xdeadbee0 is written to 0xA0243ffc. MIZAR_USB_DCFG and MIZAR_USB_DSTS are read. MIZAR_USB_DCFG is rewritten, MIZAR_USB_DCTL is written with 0x80f00a00, and MIZAR_USB_DALEPENA is written with 0xff to enable all endpoints. setup_stage() is called which sets up a TRB at event_trb_addr pointing to Buffer_PointerLO with size 0x8 and control 0x823, then issues a Start Transfer command (0x506) to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD and polls for completion, then waits for interrupt. MIZAR_USB_GUSB2PHYCFG is rewritten with 0x40002547. SET ADDRESS phase writes MIZAR_USB_DCFG with 0x480809, sets up TRB, and issues Start Transfer command on endpoint 1 (offset 0x10). Handshake polling is done on address 0xa0243ff4. enumeration() is called which performs GET DEVICE DESCRIPTOR (setup_stage, data stage with descriptor data written to Buffer_PointerLO, Start Transfer command, status_stage), GET CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR (setup_stage, data stage with configuration descriptor data, Start Transfer, status_stage), and SET CONFIGURATION (setup_stage, data stage, Start Transfer, status_stage), then GET FULL CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR (setup_stage, full 0x3c byte configuration descriptor data written to Buffer_PointerLO, Start Transfer, status_stage). Handshake polling on 0xa0243ff8. Bulk OUT transfer is initiated by setting up TRB at event_trb_addr pointing to Buffer_PointerLO_1 with size 0x40 and control 0x813, issuing Start Transfer (0x506) to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x40 (endpoint 4). After interrupt, Bulk IN transfer is initiated similarly to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x50 (endpoint 5). Final marker 0xdeadbee7 is written to 0xA0243ffc. Default_IRQHandler reads MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_MSK_STS0, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR0, reads MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT, writes back event count to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT, clears sysreg interrupt by writing 0x80000000 to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR0, and clears GIC IRQ 84.","Test Description":"This testcase validates USB Full-Speed Device mode Bulk Transfer operation. It performs a soft reset of the USB controller, configures the USB2 PHY, sets up the event ring, configures the global controller register for port direction, configures device settings, enables device events, and configures user control settings. It then configures all endpoints using start new configuration and set endpoint configuration commands, allocates TX resources for 8 endpoints, and enables physical endpoints. The device controller is started and system-level interrupts are enabled. The test waits for link state connect and reset events via interrupts. It then performs USB enumeration including setup stage, SET ADDRESS, GET DEVICE DESCRIPTOR, GET CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR, SET CONFIGURATION, and GET FULL CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR, each involving TRB setup, Start Transfer commands on the DEPCMD register with polling for command completion, and interrupt-driven event handling. After enumeration, Bulk OUT and Bulk IN transfers are initiated on separate endpoints by setting up TRBs and issuing Start Transfer commands. The interrupt handler reads interrupt status, processes event counts via the event count register, clears interrupt status, and clears the GIC IRQ.","Meta Test Steps / Procedure":"1. Call nic_programming() for NIC initialization. 2. Call GIC_EnableAllIRQ() to enable all IRQs. 3. Loop j=0 to 19: write 0x0 to Buffer_PointerLO + jDWORD and event_trb_addr + jDWORD to clear buffer and event TRB memory. 4. Write 0x40f00000 to MIZAR_USB_DCTL to initiate soft reset. 5. Read MIZAR_USB_DCTL and poll until value equals 0xf00000 (soft reset complete), with wait_on(5) between polls. 6. Write 0x40002407 to MIZAR_USB_GUSB2PHYCFG to configure USB2 PHY. 7. Write Default_Event_Ring_Array to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTADRLO. 8. Write 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTADRHI. 9. Write 0x30 to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTSIZ. 10. Write 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT. 11. Read MIZAR_USB_GCTL. 12. Write 0x30c12214 to MIZAR_USB_GCTL for port direction configuration. 13. Read MIZAR_USB_DCFG. 14. Write 0x480801 to MIZAR_USB_DCFG. 15. Write 0x1f to MIZAR_USB_DEVTEN to enable device events. 16. Read MIZAR_USB_GUCTL. 17. Write 0xa400010 to MIZAR_USB_GUCTL. 18. Call set_configuration(0,0,0,0x409) for START NEW CONFIGURATION command: writes 0 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1, 0 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0, 0x409 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD, polls MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD until command completes. 19. Call set_configuration(0,0x200,0x700,0x401) for endpoint 0 configuration: writes 0x700 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1, 0x200 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0, 0x401 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD, polls until complete. 20. Call set_configuration(0x10,0x200,0x2000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x10. 21. Call set_configuration(0x20,0x206,0x4000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x20. 22. Call set_configuration(0x30,0x20206,0x6000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x30. 23. Call set_configuration(0x40,0x204,0x8000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x40. 24. Call set_configuration(0x50,0x40204,0xa000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x50. 25. Call set_configuration(0x60,0x1ffa,0xc000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x60. 26. Call set_configuration(0x70,0x61ffa,0xe000700,0x401) for endpoint at offset 0x70. 27. Loop i=0 to 7: write 0x1 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0+(i0x10), write 0x402 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+(i0x10), read MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+(i0x10) and poll until command completes (not equal to 0x402), with wait_on(10) between polls. 28. Write 0x3 to MIZAR_USB_DALEPENA to enable physical endpoints 0 and 1. 29. Write 0x80f00000 to MIZAR_USB_DCTL to start device controller. 30. Write 0x80000000 to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN0 to enable sysreg interrupt. 31. Set int_pend=1 and wait in while loop with wait_on(5) for interrupt (link state connect/reset events). 32. If event_counter <= 0x4, set int_pend=1 and wait for another interrupt. 33. Write 0x480801 to MIZAR_USB_DCFG. 34. If event_counter <= 0x4, set int_pend=1 and wait for another interrupt. 35. Write 0xdeadbee0 to 0xA0243ffc (enumeration marker). 36. Read MIZAR_USB_DCFG. 37. Read MIZAR_USB_DSTS. 38. Write 0x480801 to MIZAR_USB_DCFG. 39. Write 0x80f00a00 to MIZAR_USB_DCTL. 40. Write 0xff to MIZAR_USB_DALEPENA to enable all physical endpoints. 41. Print Buffer_PointerLO value. 42. Call wait_on(5000). 43. Call setup_stage(): write Buffer_PointerLO to event_trb_addr, write 0x8 to event_trb_addr+0x8, write 0x823 to event_trb_addr+0xc, write event_trb_addr to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1, write 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0, write 0x506 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD, poll MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD until not 0x506 with wait_on(10), set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 44. Write 0x40002547 to MIZAR_USB_GUSB2PHYCFG. 45. If event_counter <= 0x4, set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt (twice). 46. Write 0x480809 to MIZAR_USB_DCFG (SET ADDRESS). 47. Write Buffer_PointerLO to event_trb_addr, write 0x0 to event_trb_addr+0x8, write 0x853 to event_trb_addr+0xc. 48. Write event_trb_addr to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1+0x10, write 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0+0x10. 49. Write 0x506 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x10, poll until not 0x506 with wait_on(10). 50. If event_counter <= 0x4, set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 51. Set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 52. Poll 0xa0243ff4 until non-zero (handshake). 53. Call enumeration(): internally calls setup_stage(), writes marker 0xdeadbee1 to 0xA0243ffc, waits for interrupt, sets up GET DEVICE DESCRIPTOR TRB (size 0x12, control 0x853), writes device descriptor data to Buffer_PointerLO (0x02000012, 0x40000000, etc.), issues Start Transfer on MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x10, polls for completion, waits for interrupts, calls status_stage(). Then calls setup_stage() for GET CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR, writes marker 0xdeadbee3, sets up TRB (size 0x9, control 0x853), writes configuration descriptor data to Buffer_PointerLO (0x003c0209, 0xe0000101, 0x00000032), issues Start Transfer on MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x10, polls, waits for interrupts, calls status_stage(). Then calls setup_stage() for SET CONFIGURATION, writes marker 0xdeadbee4, sets up TRB (size 0x0, control 0x853), writes 0x00 to Buffer_PointerLO, issues Start Transfer, polls, waits for interrupts. Then calls setup_stage() for GET FULL CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR, writes marker 0xdeadbee5, sets up TRB (size 0x3c, control 0x853), writes full configuration descriptor data (15 DWORDs) to Buffer_PointerLO, issues Start Transfer on MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x10, polls, waits for interrupts, calls status_stage(). 54. Poll 0xa0243ff8 until non-zero (handshake). 55. Write 0xdeadbee6 to 0xA0243ffc. 56. Set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 57. Set up Bulk OUT TRB: write Buffer_PointerLO_1 to event_trb_addr, write 0x40 to event_trb_addr+0x8, write 0x813 to event_trb_addr+0xc. 58. Write event_trb_addr to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1+0x40, write 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0+0x40. 59. Write 0x506 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x40, poll until not 0x506 with wait_on(10). 60. Set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 61. Set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 62. Set up Bulk IN TRB: write Buffer_PointerLO_1 to event_trb_addr, write 0x40 to event_trb_addr+0x8, write 0x813 to event_trb_addr+0xc. 63. Write event_trb_addr to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1+0x50, write 0x0 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0+0x50. 64. Write 0x506 to MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD+0x50, poll until not 0x506 with wait_on(10). 65. Set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 66. Write 0xdeadbee7 to 0xA0243ffc (final marker). 67. Set int_pend=1 and wait for interrupt. 68. Call finish(0). IRQ Handler (Default_IRQHandler): clear int_pend to 0, read MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_MSK_STS0, read MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR0, read MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT, store event_count in event_counter, write event_count back to MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT, if rd_data && 0x80000000 then write 0x80000000 to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR0, call GIC_ClearIRQ(84).","Test Steps / Procedure":"1. Initialize NIC programming and enable all GIC IRQs. 2. Clear buffer pointer and event TRB memory regions (20 entries each). 3. Perform USB controller soft reset by writing to DCTL and poll until reset completes. 4. Configure USB2 PHY settings. 5. Set up the event ring by configuring event address low, event address high, event size, and event count registers. 6. Configure the global controller register for port direction. 7. Configure device settings and enable device events via DEVTEN register. 8. Configure user control settings via GUCTL register. 9. Issue Start New Configuration command and configure 8 endpoints using endpoint command registers (DEPCMDPAR0, DEPCMDPAR1, DEPCMD) with polling for command completion. 10. Allocate TX resources for 8 endpoints by writing to DEPCMDPAR0 and DEPCMD in a loop, polling for completion. 11. Enable physical endpoints 0 and 1 via DALEPENA register. 12. Start the device controller by writing to DCTL. 13. Enable system-level interrupt. 14. Wait for link state connect and reset events via interrupt-driven mechanism. 15. Read device status from DSTS register and reconfigure device settings. 16. Enable all physical endpoints via DALEPENA register. 17. Execute setup stage: prepare TRB, issue Start Transfer command on DEPCMD, poll for completion, wait for interrupt. 18. Reconfigure USB2 PHY and wait for interrupts. 19. Perform SET ADDRESS by updating device configuration and issuing Start Transfer command on endpoint 1. 20. Poll handshake register until ready. 21. Execute enumeration sequence: GET DEVICE DESCRIPTOR (setup, data with descriptor payload, status), GET CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR (setup, data, status), SET CONFIGURATION (setup, data, status), GET FULL CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR (setup, data with full descriptor payload, status). 22. Poll second handshake register until ready. 23. Initiate Bulk OUT transfer: set up TRB with buffer and size, issue Start Transfer on Bulk OUT endpoint, wait for interrupt completion. 24. Initiate Bulk IN transfer: set up TRB with buffer and size, issue Start Transfer on Bulk IN endpoint, wait for interrupt completion. 25. Write final completion marker and wait for final interrupt. 26. Call finish to end the test.","Meta Impacted Registers":"Buffer_PointerLO; event_trb_addr; MIZAR_USB_DCTL; MIZAR_USB_GUSB2PHYCFG; MIZAR_USB_GEVNTADRLO; MIZAR_USB_GEVNTADRHI; MIZAR_USB_GEVNTSIZ; MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT; MIZAR_USB_GCTL; MIZAR_USB_DCFG; MIZAR_USB_DEVTEN; MIZAR_USB_GUCTL; MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR0; MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD; MIZAR_USB_DALEPENA; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN0; 0xA0243ffc; MIZAR_USB_DSTS; MIZAR_USB_DEPCMDPAR1; 0xa0243ff4; 0xa0243ff8; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_MSK_STS0; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR0; Buffer_PointerLO_1","Impacted Registers":"DCTL; GCTL; DEVTEN; GUCTL; DEPCMDPAR0; DEPCMD; DALEPENA; DSTS","Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria":"Soft reset validation: MIZAR_USB_DCTL is polled until it reads 0xf00000, confirming soft reset completion. Endpoint command completion: MIZAR_USB_DEPCMD (at various offsets) is polled after each command write (0x409, 0x401, 0x402, 0x506) until the register value no longer equals the written command value, indicating command completion. Interrupt-driven event validation: int_pend flag is set to 1 before each wait, and the Default_IRQHandler clears int_pend to 0 upon interrupt, allowing the main flow to proceed. event_counter is updated from MIZAR_USB_GEVNTCOUNT in the IRQ handler and checked against 0x4 to determine if additional interrupt waits are needed. Handshake validation: addresses 0xa0243ff4 and 0xa0243ff8 are polled until non-zero, confirming host-side readiness. Sysreg interrupt validation: MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR0 is read and bit 31 (0x80000000) is checked; if set, it is cleared by writing 0x80000000 back. GIC IRQ 84 is cleared via GIC_ClearIRQ(84). Progress markers (0xdeadbee0 through 0xdeadbee7) are written to 0xA0243ffc at various enumeration stages. Test completes by calling finish(0).","Validation / Acceptance Criteria":"Soft reset must complete successfully as confirmed by polling DCTL until the expected reset-complete value is read. Each endpoint command (Start New Configuration, Set Endpoint Configuration, Endpoint TX Resource Allocation, Start Transfer) must complete as confirmed by polling DEPCMD until the command value clears. Interrupt-driven events must be received for link state connect, reset, and transfer completion events, with the event count register read and acknowledged in the interrupt handler. Handshake registers must return non-zero values indicating host-side readiness before proceeding with enumeration and bulk transfers. USB enumeration must complete successfully including SET ADDRESS, GET DEVICE DESCRIPTOR, GET CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR, SET CONFIGURATION, and GET FULL CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR phases. Bulk OUT and Bulk IN transfers must complete with interrupt confirmation. The test must reach finish(0) indicating successful completion.","Remarks":"Test operates in USB Full-Speed Device mode with Bulk Transfer. Interrupt-driven flow uses int_pend flag and Default_IRQHandler on GIC IRQ 84. event_counter tracks event count from the event count register and gates additional interrupt waits. Handshake polling on two memory-mapped addresses synchronizes with the host side. Progress markers are written to a memory-mapped address at each enumeration stage. The enumeration function includes GET DEVICE DESCRIPTOR, GET CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR, SET CONFIGURATION, and GET FULL CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTOR phases. Bulk transfers use separate endpoints (offset 0x40 for OUT, offset 0x50 for IN). The set_configuration helper function writes to DEPCMDPAR1, DEPCMDPAR0, and DEPCMD at parameterized offsets and polls for command completion. The status_stage helper sets up a status TRB and issues a Start Transfer command with interrupt waits. Several Agent 4 register mappings are unresolved."}]

